# Git hooks must be checked out with LF endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this repo, which would otherwise give a fresh clone
# `#!/bin/sh\r` — the trailing CR becomes part of the interpreter path and the
# hook dies with "bad interpreter: no such file or directory". The failure is
# quiet in the sense that it only shows up at commit time on a machine nobody
# tested, so pin the endings rather than relying on the checkout default.
#
# Deliberately scoped to .githooks/ only: a repo-wide normalization rule would
# re-touch every source file and is a separate decision.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
